Privacy & data: paths, counts, and the files themselves
======================================================

The page said conversations "are stored on this device", which is reassurance dressed as information.
Nothing on it told you where, what, or how much.

There is now a `/api/quixi/storage/locations` endpoint that reads the real directory and reports it:

  * the data directory path, and whether it is readable
  * counts: chats, memory drawers (.md), artifacts
  * each named file with its absolute path and size — persona.md, preferences.json, providers.json,
    voice.json — or "not created yet"

The page renders that as a path chip, three counts and a table, and says what actually leaves the
machine (the prompt and its task context, to the provider you chose) and where credentials live. The
claim it makes is the one a file system can back up: you can read, grep, back up or delete all of it
without asking the app.
diff -Naur /tmp/mk35/a37/crates/quixi-engine/src/lib.rs /tmp/mk35/b/crates/quixi-engine/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/quixi-engine/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/quixi-engine/src/lib.rs
@@ -1593,6 +1593,56 @@
         if clean_path == "/api/quixi/storage/status" {
             return Self::json_resp(200, &self.session_storage_status());
         }
+        // Where the data actually is, in paths rather than reassurance. The Privacy page shows this
+        // instead of telling people their conversations are "stored on this device" — they can read
+        // the directory, see the files, and open it in a file manager.
+        if clean_path == "/api/quixi/storage/locations" {
+            let data = self.data_dir.clone();
+            let count = |sub: &str, ext: Option<&str>| -> u64 {
+                std::fs::read_dir(data.join(sub))
+                    .map(|entries| {
+                        entries
+                            .flatten()
+                            .filter(|e| match ext {
+                                Some(want) => e.path().extension().and_then(|x| x.to_str()) == Some(want),
+                                None => e.path().is_file(),
+                            })
+                            .count() as u64
+                    })
+                    .unwrap_or(0)
+            };
+            let disk = |path: &std::path::Path| -> Value {
+                match std::fs::metadata(path) {
+                    Ok(_) => json!({ "ok": true }),
+                    Err(e) => json!({ "ok": false, "error": e.to_string() }),
+                }
+            };
+            let mut files: Vec<Value> = Vec::new();
+            for (label, rel) in [
+                ("persona", "persona.md"),
+                ("preferences", "preferences.json"),
+                ("providers", "providers.json"),
+                ("voice", "voice.json"),
+            ] {
+                let p = data.join(rel);
+                files.push(json!({
+                    "label": label,
+                    "path": p.to_string_lossy(),
+                    "exists": p.is_file(),
+                    "bytes": std::fs::metadata(&p).map(|m| m.len()).unwrap_or(0),
+                }));
+            }
+            return Self::json_resp(200, &json!({
+                "data_dir": data.to_string_lossy(),
+                "reachable": disk(&data),
+                "counts": {
+                    "chats": count("chats", Some("json")),
+                    "memory_drawers": count("memory", Some("md")),
+                    "artifacts": count("artifacts", None),
+                },
+                "files": files,
+            }));
+        }
         if clean_path == "/api/quixi/storage/retry" && method == "POST" {
             return Self::json_resp(200, &self.retry_session_saves());
         }
